{
 "version": "1.2",
 "curation_rules": [
  "1. PRODUCT BRANDS ONLY. Retailers/marketplaces (Amazon, Flipkart, Nykaa, Myntra, Ajio, Purplle, Meesho, Tata Cliq, Blinkit, Zepto, Decathlon-as-retailer) are excluded; they are tracked separately via citations. EXCEPTION: marketplace house brands that are product brands (Roadster, Sangria, Anouk, Mast & Harbour, HRX, Dressberry etc.) are included. Decathlon is included as a product brand for its own-brand shoes, canonical 'Decathlon' with aliases ['Kalenji', 'Jogflow', 'Decathlon Jogflow'].",
  "2. Product lines are grouped under the parent brand ('Plum Green Tea Pore' -> Plum; 'Nike Run Defy' -> Nike; 'CeraVe Moisturising Cream' / 'CeraVe Moisturizing Cream' -> CeraVe). Aliases include every observed surface form and spelling variant of the brand name (Levi's / Levi / Levis; Dot & Key / Dot and Key; straight and curly apostrophe forms).",
  "3. Generic, ingredient, and junk strings are excluded: ingredients ('Vitamin C', 'Ethyl Ascorbic Acid'), section headers ('Key Ingredients', 'Why it works', 'Best overall'), pronouns, Hinglish function words ('Meri', 'Kyun', 'Halanki'), fabric types ('Banarasi', 'Georgette', 'Chanderi', 'Organza', 'Kanjivaram'), and unattributable fragments ('Macs', 'Krooley', 'Kano Tapered', 'Skinn', 'Cinamide', 'Sali').",
  "4. india_origin: true for brands founded/headquartered in India. Louis Philippe, Van Heusen, Allen Solly, Peter England are Indian-owned via ABFRL and marked india_origin true; Van Heusen carries note 'abfrl_licensed' because the name is internationally licensed (PVH) but operated by an Indian company, the others are ABFRL-owned outright. CeraVe, Cetaphil, Neutrogena, Nike, Puma, Adidas, Skechers, Levi's, Wrangler, Lee, Zara, H&M are NOT India-origin. Ambiguous origins were verified with web search and carry a 'verified_via' URL.",
  "5. Alias safety: matching is case-insensitive word-boundary regex, so no alias may be a common English/Hindi word without a flag. 'W' is matched ONLY via aliases 'W for Woman' / 'W for Women', never bare 'W'. Other risky bare forms (Arrow, Plum, Simple, Soch, Lee, Libas, Minimalist, Pilgrim, Deconstruct, Hyphen, The Ordinary, Mufti, Killer, Zodiac, Numero Uno, Highlander, Roadster, Sangria, Campus, Asian, Bata, Red Tape, Snitch, Kalki, Banarasee) are kept but carry 'risky_alias': true so matches get spot-checked.",
  "6. The ENTIRE candidates file was worked through, not just the top: every candidate with responses >= 2 that is a real product brand appears. Single-response-only candidates (Suta, Nivia, Venusia, Novology, Gabit, Cult.sport, New Balance, Bene Kleed, Glitchez, SIRIL, Sidhidata, MANNAT MAkers, Yashika, Tarangini, Trendia, Maybell, The Loom) were left out. Multi-brand retailers observed in answers (Jaypore, Pernia's Pop-Up Shop, Ensemble, Saree.com, Nykaa Fashion) are excluded per rule 1.",
  "7. Every brand has category: 'skincare' | 'fashion' | 'both'.",
  "v1.1 (verification-driven, see METHODOLOGY.md deviations log): entries may carry context_regex (brand match counts only if the context pattern appears within 80 characters) or exclude_following (negative lookahead after the brand name). Applied to Simple, Asian, Lee after the adversarial risky-alias audit.",
  "v1.2 (13 Oct 2026, October re-run): 11 brands added that the October corpus names in 8 or more answers and v1.1 did not list. Added for the sensitivity check only; the primary August-vs-October comparison uses v1.1 on both waves."
 ],
